anically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"swe-agent/swe-rex","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6d2da894b45d49ea8b7db90d982c13e6"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_65b7ca57b7e04f54978d8e21dbd08f485533eae2ea969aa8c1e0e7a438c09007"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Deployment classes start the target environment (e.g. a Docker container or AWS instance) and hand back a RemoteRuntime instance as the main interface for interacting with the environment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2c20d571421fb60071f751de608eb7a21801a80ff28e944bb806d40a4832008"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Because LocalRuntime can be used directly when code runs locally or in a sandboxed environment, the framework appears to support fully local usage without a remote deployment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fca8982ef3065dd80bfa6153eda29e1ffd6dd3c6ddcb626f0e2906a25e96411c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Runtime class provides file read/write methods, an execute method for arbitrary commands, and a run_in_session method to run commands in an existing shell or interactive session."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fe5a5f4c8a1acaddc566865581f95a952cc0ee40235826056be2a4121408208a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A FastAPI server inside the container forwards requests from RemoteRuntime to LocalRuntime, which actually executes commands; the two classes share the same interface, are interchangeable, and exceptions from LocalRuntime are transferred transparently."}],"claim_ids":["clm_65b7ca57b7e04f54978d8e21dbd08f485533eae2ea969aa8c1e0e7a438c09007","clm_d2c20d571421fb60071f751de608eb7a21801a80ff28e944bb806d40a4832008","clm_fca8982ef3065dd80bfa6153eda29e1ffd6dd3c6ddcb626f0e2906a25e96411c","clm_fe5a5f4c8a1acaddc566865581f95a952cc0ee40235826056be2a4121408208a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_6d2da894b45d49ea8b7db90d982c13e6","id":"pg_8a980d37bbc458b48c27352a78a25699","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/swe-agent-swe-rex-docs-architecture-md-5c995c365dfb-352a78a25699.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_17214af7ae105af48f573b3cafa9284d"],"title":"SWE-agent/SWE-ReX/docs/architecture.md @ 5c995c365dfb","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6d2da894b45d49ea8b7db90d982c13e6"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_13be2bd5dca4ca4b2a53cc04f88b8a5bb2f50c629f9f146f750d1b03d359389c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"SWE-ReX exposes a runtime interface for interacting with sandboxed shell environments, letting an AI agent run arbitrary commands on arbitrary environments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c125130d14929067f1b29e0a3a8139b8ae2cc7a95f969b3db26c7bde99c7955"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"SWE-ReX detects when shell commands finish, extracts output and exit code for the agent, supports interactive tools like ipython and gdb, and allows multiple parallel shell sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_445b71d725136ff071170149f409608a1e9a8249d2949602824188875d27eea9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project advertises fast, massively parallel agent runs, citing large-benchmark evaluation and a demo of SWE-agent running on 30 SWE-bench instances in parallel."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5e6f5b67bc5ad37ea6c55e0261fba661529fcabeae8c2039d558481c1ea6b606"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package installs via pip as swe-rex, with optional extras for modal, fargate, and daytona, plus a dev extra for development setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_676de505113dc5cf97e52690cb4429cf449013796825a64325754d909d618429"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"SWE-ReX originated from the SWE-agent and SWE-agent enigma projects and aims to disentangle agent logic from infrastructure concerns."},{"claim_ids":["clm_97e3728d64d8e71b86e80ee6f665c875bb3f1e469962092042b26f1bef08bdb4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent code stays the same regardless of whether commands run locally, in Docker containers, on AWS remote machines, Modal, or other backends."}],"claim_ids":["clm_13be2bd5dca4ca4b2a53cc04f88b8a5bb2f50c629f9f146f750d1b03d359389c","clm_3c125130d14929067f1b29e0a3a8139b8ae2cc7a95f969b3db26c7bde99c7955","clm_445b71d725136ff071170149f409608a1e9a8249d2949602824188875d27eea9","clm_5e6f5b67bc5ad37ea6c55e0261fba661529fcabeae8c2039d558481c1ea6b606","clm_676de505113dc5cf97e52690cb4429cf449013796825a64325754d909d618429","clm_97e3728d64d8e71b86e80ee6f665c875bb3f1e469962092042b26f1bef08bdb4"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_6d2da894b45d49ea8b7db90d982c13e6","id":"pg_942ac4a9097b5bed8060d53adfa811b4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/swe-agent-swe-rex-readme-md-5c995c365dfb-d53adfa811b4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_472b7f295443531c80d668db702ff376"],"title":"SWE-agent/SWE-ReX/README.md @ 5c995c365dfb","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:24:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6d2da894b45d49ea8b7db90d982c13e6"}
